  "vector_memory": {
    "semantic_summary": "The ResponseParser class is a critical service layer component designed to ingest raw, unstructured strings from an LLM and transform them into a canonical Python dictionary model. It specializes in extracting structured data, prioritizing XML parsing, but falling back to robust regex-based field extraction if the primary structure is corrupted. Its core function is to reliably capture 'thought', 'action', 'manifest', and 'response_to_user' fields regardless of LLM formatting inconsistencies."
  },
